# Code Conventions

## Components

- Functional components + hooks ONLY (no class components)
- Props: `type {ComponentName}Props` (named pattern; prefer `type`, not `interface`)
- Named exports only (no default exports)
- Colocated tests: `ComponentName.test.tsx`

## TypeScript

- Strict mode — no `any`, no `@ts-ignore`
- Prefer `type` over `interface` for simple types
- Import types: `import type { X } from "..."`

## Files

- kebab-case for files: `element-utils.ts`
- PascalCase for components: `LayerUI.tsx`

## How to verify

From the repository root:

- **Types:** `yarn test:typecheck`
- **Lint:** `yarn test:code`
- **Prettier (format):** `yarn test:other`
- **Unit / component tests (Vitest):** `yarn test` (or `yarn test:app --watch=false` for a single non-watch run)
- **Full CI-style check:** `yarn test:all` (typecheck + eslint + prettier + app tests)
- **Manual:** `yarn start`, then exercise the changed flows in the browser (port **3000** or `VITE_APP_PORT`)

After changing `packages/excalidraw`, prefer at least typecheck + tests related to your edit before opening a PR.
